    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm trying to fix my lawn. it looks pretty yellow and thin in some spots. can you explain what those NPK numbers on fertilizer bags actually stand for? also what does it look like if the grass is missing phosphorus?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The NPK numbers on fertilizer bags represent the percentage by weight of three primary macronutrients: Nitrogen (N), Phosphate (P), and Potassium (K). Nitrogen promotes leafy green growth, while Phosphorus is crucial for strong roots and flower/seed production. If your grass is missing phosphorus, you might notice yellowing leaves with purplish-red tints, especially on the base of the plant.",
